% Add your BibTeX publication entries here.
%
% The home page renders EVERY entry in this file as ONE FLAT LIST, in the ORDER
% OF THIS FILE — there is no year grouping any more (see the
% {% bibliography --group_by none %} call at the bottom of _pages/about.md).
% So: put the newest work at the top, and there is nothing else to configure.
%
% Why passing --group_by none is enough: jekyll-scholar only reorders entries
% when `scholar.sort_by` is set, and it is not set here, so the file order is
% preserved as written.
%
% selected = {true} is kept only as a "highlighted" marker; it does NOT affect
% rendering right now. To go back to showing only the highlighted entries, swap
% the {% bibliography --group_by none %} call in _pages/about.md for
% {% include selected_papers.liquid %}.
%
% Do NOT wrap your own name in \textbf{} or \underline{}: the theme already detects it
% from `scholar.first_name` / `scholar.last_name` in _config.yml and marks it itself.
% LaTeX commands here are not converted, so they leak into the page as literal text.
%
% Optional fields, each one adds a button under the entry:
%   preview = {file.png}       -> thumbnail, read from /assets/img/publication_preview/.
%                                 A full https://... URL, or a video (.mp4/.webm/.ogg/.mov),
%                                 also works.
%   bibtex_show = {true}       -> "Bib" button, expands the raw BibTeX inline
%   doi = {10.xxxx/yyyy}       -> "DOI" button
%   arxiv = {2502.04638}       -> "arXiv" button
%   html = {https://...}       -> "HTML" button (a bare path is resolved under /assets/html/)
%   pdf = {https://...}        -> "PDF" button (a bare path is resolved under /assets/pdf/)
%   code = {https://...}       -> "Code" button
%   website = {https://...}    -> "Website" button
%   video / poster / slides / supp / blog / hal  -> same pattern
%   abstract = {...}           -> "Abs" button, expands the abstract inline
%   award = {...}              -> award badge
% A trailing marker on a surname ("Yeh, Christopher*") is rendered as a superscript,
% which is the usual way to flag equal contribution. It does not affect self-detection.
%
% --- Adding a thumbnail -----------------------------------------------------
% 1. Drop the image into assets/img/publication_preview/ (this is the only folder
%    the theme looks in). Name it lowercase-with-hyphens, no spaces:
%    my-paper.jpg, not "My Paper.JPG".
% 2. Add one line to the entry:  preview={my-paper.jpg},
% 3. Rebuild. No HTML, no CSS, no width attribute needed — the theme renders it in
%    a fixed left column (col-sm-2) and it opens fullscreen on click.
% Size: long edge around 800 px, file under ~100 KB. Everything in that folder was
% normalized with .workbuddy/compress_previews.py (long edge 800 px, JPEG q85,
% originals kept in .workbuddy/backup-*/preview-orig/) — re-run it after dropping
% new images in.
% Note: rendered height follows each image's aspect ratio (the theme has no
% fixed-height CSS for .preview), so very different ratios look ragged.
% Entries WITHOUT a preview are fine too: they just render the text full-width.

